                <pb facs="0567" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg485"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/1619.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the American Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-05-16"><hi rendition="#italic">May 16,
                        1911</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 344.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 509,
                    of the 29th ultimo, transmitting copies of two notes in which you requested the
                    foreign office to cause American citizens and property at Parral to be
                    protected, with one of which you inclosed a copy of a letter from the manager of
                    the West Mexican Mines (Ltd.).</p>
                <p>Your action in addressing these notes to the foreign office is approved by the
                    Department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
